(7391488, 1160392, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by h2:</b></div><hr/><i> might have worked better with slightly different backgrounds, otherwise good shot(s) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How would of this worked better with a different background, baffles me. Perfect for me Penny.</td>', 'Originally posted by h2: might have worked better with slightly different backgrounds, otherwise good shot(s)   How would of this worked better with a different background, baffles me. Perfect for me Penny.', '2015-07-23 01:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7391523, 1160438, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m back to look again... because I totally LOVE this idea of yours... and how you achieved portraying it.<br/> <br/>Even the TITLE is magnificent!  LOL!<br/> <br/>Congratulations again... and on a new personal Best!   Yipppeee! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m so flattered, Lydia.  The idea didn''t come to me fully formed.  As I looked at the example photos I couldn''t conceive of how he could come up with the fully formed idea and decided that he had to start with one photo/object and then extrapolate.  So, I got in my car and went for a drive looking for anything I could draw a line through and add something to the top.  It''s amazing how many things there are that fit this.  I was actually driving down a back road to try and get a shot of some power plant cooling towers when I saw this mowed path in a field and immediately thought "Razor!!".  Had I not been looking with eyes fixed on that idea I''d never have come up with this on my own.</td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: I''m back to look again... because I totally LOVE this idea of yours... and how you achieved portraying it. Even the TITLE is magnificent!  LOL! Congratulations again... and on a new personal Best!   Yipppeee!   I''m so flattered, Lydia.  The idea didn''t come to me fully formed.  As I looked at the example photos I couldn''t conceive of how he could come up with the fully formed idea and decided that he had to start with one photo/object and then extrapolate.  So, I got in my car and went for a drive looking for anything I could draw a line through and add something to the top.  It''s amazing how many things there are that fit this.  I was actually driving down a back road to try and get a shot of some power plant cooling towers when I saw this mowed path in a field and immediately thought "Razor!!".  Had I not been looking with eyes fixed on that idea I''d never have come up with this on my own.', '2015-07-23 07:52:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7391524, 1160450, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>A very impressive shot that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>What a fun challenge this was! I have not come across this concept before, I have to say what a great idea it is to introduce a fun element into your images. Your images have taken two straightforward ideas and transformed them into something with a completely new dimension.<br/> <br/>The lower image is a quite standard landscape with what looks as though it may be the base of a wind turbine? I agree with one of your commenters there are some distracting elements but in the context of the combined images these are quite minor and do not impact on the end result. The upper image is very well done apart from some overexposure at the top of the ball which again in the context of the end result is quite minor.<br/> <br/>The idea is quite simple and straightforward but very effective and has been well received here with a very respectable score and lots of positive comments all of whom I agree with. Well done and thank you for an excellent submission, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* A very impressive shot that meets the challenge well. What a fun challenge this was! I have not come across this concept before, I have to say what a great idea it is to introduce a fun element into your images. Your images have taken two straightforward ideas and transformed them into something with a completely new dimension. The lower image is a quite standard landscape with what looks as though it may be the base of a wind turbine? I agree with one of your commenters there are some distracting elements but in the context of the combined images these are quite minor and do not impact on the end result. The upper image is very well done apart from some overexposure at the top of the ball which again in the context of the end result is quite minor. The idea is quite simple and straightforward but very effective and has been well received here with a very respectable score and lots of positive comments all of whom I agree with. Well done and thank you for an excellent submission, Sid', '2015-07-23 07:56:24.000000', NULL, 0),
